<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#persian-language">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persian language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Persian is an Iranian language spoken mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and Tajikistan, whose literary form developed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Islamic conquest</a> from earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Middle Persian</a>. It became a prestige language of administration and culture across much of the Islamic world. Persian traditions passed from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> into the Abbasid state, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> used Persian as its language of government.</p></div>
